cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Reproducible Ray-Tracing Pipeline for 5G NR Multicell Digital Twins: From Public 3D City Data to an Interactive Artefact"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
authors:
  - family-names: Yenamandra
    given-names: Rao S.
    affiliation: "DigitalTwinSim"
  - family-names: Lalwani
    given-names: Sameer
    affiliation: "DigitalTwinSim"
  - family-names: Nsofu
    given-names: Mubanga
    affiliation: "Vodacom SA, Midrand, South Africa"
  - family-names: Ram
    given-names: Asokan
    affiliation: "Wireless Research Centre, Wake Forest, NC, USA"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24210760"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ysrao/twin5GNR-multicell-SF"
url: "https://ysrao.github.io/twin5GNR-multicell-SF/twin5GNR-multicell-SionnaRT-OpenScene-Nov14.html"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible 5G NR multicell ray-tracing package: a three-site,
  nine-sector layout at 3.6 GHz traced with Sionna RT over a downtown
  San Francisco city tile built from open municipal data (DataSF building
  footprints with LiDAR heights), runnable end-to-end on a free Colab T4 with
  reader-local data, with CSV-driven tower-shift experiments and an
  interactive artefact wired to the trace output. Includes a controlled
  sensitivity analysis showing the coverage result is a property of the
  scene rather than of solver configuration, and that a scene can pass on
  path existence while failing on path strength.
keywords:
  - 5G NR
  - ray tracing
  - Sionna RT
  - digital twin
  - radio propagation
  - open educational resource
